{"The `if client_sample_rate:` truthiness check in _set_sample_rate_from_error_sampling skips the valid value 0.0, leaving sample_rate unset for zero-rate configurations": 0.532639741897583, "_get_event_stats uses outer `dataset` variable instead of the `scoped_dataset` parameter when calling is_errors_query_for_error_upsampled_projects, causing incorrect upsampling decisions when callers pass different scoped datasets": 0.9779760241508484, "upsampled_count SnQL function is only registered in the Discover dataset's function_converter, so queries routed to other datasets (e.g., errors) will fail to resolve it": 0.9599429965019226, "60-second cache on the allowlist eligibility check can become stale, causing upsampling to be applied when sample_weight doesn't exist or skipped when it should apply": 0.5546932816505432, "New SnQLFunction 'upsampled_count' has default_result_type set to 'number' but should likely be 'integer' since it wraps toInt64(sum(...)), causing potential type inconsistencies in API responses": 0.6869862079620361, "Broad `except Exception: pass` in _set_sample_rate_from_error_sampling silently swallows unexpected errors": 0.4473094344139099}